1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,133
In this video you will learn to manage user profiles, link them to a Nintendo

2
00:00:05,133 --> 00:00:10,200
Account without internet, and move profiles with their play hours to another

3
00:00:10,200 --> 00:00:12,200
console.

4
00:00:12,200 --> 00:00:14,867
On the Tools tab open Tools, then Users.

5
00:00:14,867 --> 00:00:18,333
Each profile shows its avatar, name and link status.

6
00:00:18,333 --> 00:00:22,267
Green Linked means the profile has a Nintendo Account link.

7
00:00:22,267 --> 00:00:24,467
Red Not linked means it has none.

8
00:00:24,467 --> 00:00:27,667
A grey status means Kefir Hub could not read it.

9
00:00:27,667 --> 00:00:31,000
A or Plus opens the menu for the selected profile.

10
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:34,867
X marks a profile, Y inverts the marks, and B clears them.

11
00:00:34,867 --> 00:00:37,333
To add a profile, choose Create user.

12
00:00:37,333 --> 00:00:41,067
The system's own creator opens: pick a name and an icon.

13
00:00:41,067 --> 00:00:43,667
A console holds at most eight profiles.

14
00:00:43,667 --> 00:00:47,933
To change a name, select the profile, press A and choose Rename.

15
00:00:47,933 --> 00:00:49,933
Type the new name and confirm.

16
00:00:49,933 --> 00:00:54,200
A name holds at most 15 Cyrillic letters or 31 Latin characters.

17
00:00:54,200 --> 00:00:56,800
A longer name is cut without a warning.

18
00:00:56,800 --> 00:00:59,333
For a new avatar choose Change avatar.

19
00:00:59,333 --> 00:01:04,533
You can take another profile's avatar, a picture from the config/kefir/avatars

20
00:01:04,533 --> 00:01:07,800
folder, or any image on the card through From SD.

21
00:01:07,800 --> 00:01:13,133
The SteamGridDB tile finds icons by game name; it needs internet and an API key.

22
00:01:13,133 --> 00:01:16,667
The new avatar shows on the HOME Menu after a reboot.

23
00:01:16,667 --> 00:01:18,667
Choose Reboot or Later.

24
00:01:18,667 --> 00:01:22,067
To delete a profile, choose Delete user and hold A.

25
00:01:22,067 --> 00:01:25,067
The profile's game saves are deleted with it.

26
00:01:25,067 --> 00:01:27,133
At least one profile must stay.

27
00:01:27,133 --> 00:01:31,933
Kefir Hub offers to back up all profiles first, and then the game saves.

28
00:01:31,933 --> 00:01:35,600
Choose Choose saves, mark the games with X and press A.

29
00:01:35,600 --> 00:01:40,667
Deleting cannot be undone, and restoring the profile from that backup is not

30
00:01:40,667 --> 00:01:42,667
available yet.

31
00:01:42,667 --> 00:01:46,467
So make sure you back up the game saves you want to keep.

32
00:01:46,467 --> 00:01:48,467
Now the link.

33
00:01:48,467 --> 00:01:53,667
Some games refuse to start unless the profile is linked to a Nintendo Account.

34
00:01:53,667 --> 00:01:56,000
They only check that a link exists.

35
00:01:56,000 --> 00:02:00,867
Kefir Hub can create one without internet, using built-in donor accounts.

36
00:02:00,867 --> 00:02:03,800
Every Not linked profile gets its own donor.

37
00:02:03,800 --> 00:02:08,933
Profiles that are already linked are not changed, and neither are game saves.

38
00:02:08,933 --> 00:02:12,733
Before writing, Kefir Hub keeps a copy of the link files.

39
00:02:12,733 --> 00:02:17,467
Press A, choose Link Nintendo Account and confirm with Link and reboot.

40
00:02:17,467 --> 00:02:22,267
The console reboots right away, and afterwards the profiles show Linked.

41
00:02:22,267 --> 00:02:25,800
Important: a donor link is not your Nintendo Account.

42
00:02:25,800 --> 00:02:30,000
The same donor accounts are built into every copy of Kefir Hub.

43
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:32,533
Warning: this link carries a ban risk.

44
00:02:32,533 --> 00:02:37,200
It works only because the console is isolated from Nintendo's servers.

45
00:02:37,200 --> 00:02:41,600
Use it only on an emuMMC that is isolated from Nintendo's servers.

46
00:02:41,600 --> 00:02:47,133
To remove a link, mark the profiles with X and choose Unlink Nintendo Account, then

47
00:02:47,133 --> 00:02:49,133
Unlink and reboot.

48
00:02:49,133 --> 00:02:51,667
With nothing marked, all are unlinked.

49
00:02:51,667 --> 00:02:55,067
Careful: this removes any link, a real account too.

50
00:02:55,067 --> 00:03:00,533
If you unlinked a real account on emuMMC, link the profile again through Kefir Hub

51
00:03:00,533 --> 00:03:04,267
with Link Nintendo Account, not through System Settings.

52
00:03:04,267 --> 00:03:08,533
If there are unlinked profiles at launch, Kefir Hub reminds you.

53
00:03:08,533 --> 00:03:14,000
Link and reboot links them, Later asks next time, and Don't remind again turns the

54
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:16,000
reminder off.

55
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:18,000
Now moving to another console.

56
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:23,067
All profiles move with the same user IDs and, if you want, their play hours.

57
00:03:23,067 --> 00:03:28,467
So save backups from the old console restore to the same profiles on the new one.

58
00:03:28,467 --> 00:03:34,067
On the old console open Users, press A and choose Backup profiles & play hours, then

59
00:03:34,067 --> 00:03:36,067
Backup.

60
00:03:36,067 --> 00:03:41,333
If the console restarts into TegraExplorer, let it finish, start Kefir and open

61
00:03:41,333 --> 00:03:43,333
Kefir Hub again.

62
00:03:43,333 --> 00:03:48,867
Then on the Tools tab open Console Transfer and choose Share Profiles & Play Hours.

63
00:03:48,867 --> 00:03:52,000
A screen with an address and a QR code appears.

64
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:55,867
Write down the IP address: you type it on the new console.

65
00:03:55,867 --> 00:03:59,133
Keep this screen open until the transfer is done.

66
00:03:59,133 --> 00:04:01,133
A warning.

67
00:04:01,133 --> 00:04:06,600
The new console loses all its own profiles: they are replaced by the ones from the

68
00:04:06,600 --> 00:04:08,600
old console.

69
00:04:08,600 --> 00:04:11,933
With play hours, its play history is replaced too.

70
00:04:11,933 --> 00:04:14,400
Make a SYSTEM backup in hekate first.

71
00:04:14,400 --> 00:04:19,667
On the new console open Users, press A and choose Restore from another console.

72
00:04:19,667 --> 00:04:21,933
Type the old console's IP address.

73
00:04:21,933 --> 00:04:25,933
The first part of your network address is already filled in.

74
00:04:25,933 --> 00:04:30,733
Kefir Hub tests the connection and lists the backups on the old console.

75
00:04:30,733 --> 00:04:32,733
Choose one.

76
00:04:32,733 --> 00:04:35,733
It is saved to the new console's memory card.

77
00:04:35,733 --> 00:04:40,267
Now choose what to restore: Profiles only, or Profiles + play hours.

78
00:04:40,267 --> 00:04:42,267
Press Launch TegraExplorer.

79
00:04:42,267 --> 00:04:47,667
The console restarts into TegraExplorer, writes the backup and returns to hekate.

80
00:04:47,667 --> 00:04:50,333
Do not touch the console while it works.

81
00:04:50,333 --> 00:04:52,400
Start Kefir and open Kefir Hub.

82
00:04:52,400 --> 00:04:54,933
It shows whether the restore finished.

83
00:04:54,933 --> 00:05:00,000
The restore goes to the system you started Kefir Hub from, emuMMC or sysMMC.

84
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:05,333
Games and the saves themselves do not move this way: moving saves would take too

85
00:05:05,333 --> 00:05:07,333
long.

86
00:05:07,333 --> 00:05:12,733
Back up the saves in Saves, move the backups with Share Save Backups, and install

87
00:05:12,733 --> 00:05:15,067
the games on the new console again.

88
00:05:15,067 --> 00:05:17,867
All profile backups are in Manage Backups.

89
00:05:17,867 --> 00:05:23,333
Without a network, copy the backup file from the config/kefir/nand_transfer folder

90
00:05:23,333 --> 00:05:28,600
to the same folder on the new console and choose Restore profiles & play hours.

91
00:05:28,600 --> 00:05:33,600
If the console does not boot after a restore, open Payloads in hekate, then

92
00:05:33,600 --> 00:05:37,600
TegraExplorer, and run the script Undo_restore_if_wont_boot.

93
00:05:37,600 --> 00:05:39,600
It puts the old profiles back.

94
00:05:39,600 --> 00:05:43,533
If that does not help, restore the SYSTEM backup in hekate.

95
00:05:43,533 --> 00:05:48,333
Read more on the Users and Console Transfer pages of the Kefir Hub docs.
